WEBVTT

00:00.980 --> 00:03.480
<b>COOL, THANKS. LOOKING FORWARD
TO SOME GREAT ACTING.</b>

00:03.480 --> 00:06.190
Stupid Senpai.

00:09.770 --> 00:12.060
Maybe I'll just ditch him.

00:14.360 --> 00:18.120
No, of course I'm going. I love this job.

00:18.670 --> 00:21.580
<i>Senpai doesn't understand a thing.</i>

00:21.580 --> 00:25.130
<i>He never listens to what I'm saying.</i>

00:25.130 --> 00:28.090
<i>He never takes me seriously at all.</i>

00:28.680 --> 00:33.910
<i>I mean, it's just as much my fault 
for playing it all off as a joke.</i>

00:34.200 --> 00:38.300
<i>He only ever takes me seriously 
when it comes to work.</i>

00:39.030 --> 00:41.560
<i>Yet Mashiro-senpai has him 
swaying like a young leaf!</i>

00:42.230 --> 00:48.360
<i>But what bugs me most of all is this saccharine 
persona that my jealousy has me stuck in.</i>

00:49.340 --> 00:51.440
<i>What the heck am I doing?!</i>

00:55.100 --> 00:56.430
Iroha-chan?

00:58.090 --> 00:59.760
Wh-What's wrong?

01:27.690 --> 01:33.360
<b>MY FRIEND'S LITTLE SISTER HAS IT IN FOR ME!</b>

02:33.660 --> 02:35.180
What are you doing here?

02:33.670 --> 02:38.630
<b>#09 "MY FAKE GIRLFRIEND GETS TOUGH
WHEN I RESPOND TO HER CONFESSION"</b>

02:36.380 --> 02:38.500
I mean... classes are over.

02:39.230 --> 02:45.610
Oh... Well, my class ran a little late, so I 
was just surprised you were still around!

02:46.060 --> 02:48.180
I was just stopping by the library.

02:48.710 --> 02:52.400
Wow, those look so sparkly and cute! 
I bet everyone loves them!

02:52.400 --> 02:53.660
Y-Yeah.

02:53.660 --> 02:57.340
Wow, so that's the kind of stuff you read, huh?

02:57.340 --> 03:00.700
I thought you'd be more the 
"LOL, stupid normies" type.

03:01.150 --> 03:03.540
I used to feel that way,

03:03.540 --> 03:07.440
but I thought I'd try something new. 
For reference.

03:07.440 --> 03:09.060
Reference?

03:09.060 --> 03:11.400
N-Nothing! Never mind!

03:11.400 --> 03:13.710
<i>Yeah, she's hiding something!</i>

03:13.710 --> 03:16.600
H-Hey, Iroha-chan, since I found you here...

03:16.600 --> 03:17.670
Want to walk home together?

03:17.950 --> 03:20.050
Huh? Oh, uh...

03:20.050 --> 03:24.360
<i>I'm meeting Senpai in the park 
so we can go record in Otoi-san's studio!</i>

03:24.360 --> 03:25.680
<i>But I can't tell her that.</i>

03:26.010 --> 03:29.570
Uh, sorry! I have a part-time job to get to.

03:29.570 --> 03:30.360
You do?

03:30.360 --> 03:33.800
It's a secret. Something I can't 
talk about to other people.

03:33.800 --> 03:35.940
A job you can't talk about? What is it?

03:36.900 --> 03:40.490
It... involves... using... my... mouth.

03:40.490 --> 03:43.410
Your mouth? You mean...

03:43.410 --> 03:44.490
Wh-What?!

03:44.490 --> 03:48.780
Hey! Are you thinking about 
something dirty? Please!

03:48.780 --> 03:52.370
I'm a good, proper high school girl! 
I wouldn't do any shady work!

03:52.940 --> 03:55.420
Would you like to give it a try, too?

03:55.740 --> 04:00.010
N-No, that's okay! I'm busy with other things!

04:00.010 --> 04:01.880
Oh, really? That's too bad!

04:02.240 --> 04:05.180
S-Sorry to hold you up when you're busy.

04:05.180 --> 04:06.850
See you tomorrow.

04:06.850 --> 04:08.730
Yep! See ya!

04:10.520 --> 04:12.640
<i>Mashiro-senpai's so lucky.</i>

04:13.110 --> 04:18.070
<i>Senpai takes her so seriously, 
even without work factoring in.</i>

04:18.660 --> 04:20.440
<i>Work, huh?</i>

04:20.440 --> 04:25.060
<i>The studio I'm headed to is a place 
where I can let my true self out.</i>

04:25.060 --> 04:29.080
<i>I wonder how I'm actually 
supposed to behave there.</i>

04:35.490 --> 04:37.630
Is something wrong, Senpai?

04:41.060 --> 04:43.340
Nope. Not at all.

04:43.700 --> 04:45.340
I'm glad to hear that.

04:47.580 --> 04:49.270
Well, ready to go?

04:59.710 --> 05:00.690
Hey, Iroha!

05:02.070 --> 05:03.690
Yes, Senpai?

05:05.700 --> 05:09.090
How long are you gonna keep up 
this ridiculous facade?

05:09.090 --> 05:11.140
I'm not sure what you mean.

05:11.140 --> 05:16.120
This is the way I am 
24 hours a day, 365 days a year.

05:16.120 --> 05:17.540
Why are you being so stubborn?!

05:17.540 --> 05:20.830
Just go back to your evil cackle 
and aggravating lines already!

05:20.830 --> 05:23.710
I'm not being stubborn. And I refuse.

05:23.710 --> 05:26.690
I said, drop the facade and 
go back to messing with me!

05:26.690 --> 05:28.300
You should really stop.

05:26.970 --> 05:32.720
<b>GRRR</b>

05:28.300 --> 05:33.230
I may grace you with my utmost hospitality, 
but I would never mess with you.

05:33.230 --> 05:35.260
Ugh, you are so stubborn!

05:35.260 --> 05:37.600
Stop being non-annoying! It's annoying as hell!

05:37.600 --> 05:39.970
You're the one being stubborn.

05:39.970 --> 05:43.890
A sweet, shy, docile girl 
is trying to get closer to you.

05:43.890 --> 05:45.850
What problem could you have with that?

05:46.610 --> 05:49.410
Yeah, that's right! 
I don't have a problem at all!

05:49.410 --> 05:51.230
At least I shouldn't, damn it!

05:51.230 --> 05:53.360
Then everything is fine, right?

05:53.360 --> 05:56.320
Please stop saying nonsense. Hmph!

06:00.600 --> 06:03.340
Oh, you're here. Hey.

06:03.630 --> 06:06.370
I told you to quit forcing through 
rush requests, didn't I?

06:06.370 --> 06:07.910
I oughta pound you one.

06:08.450 --> 06:10.100
Not that it matters, I guess.

06:10.100 --> 06:12.680
We're sorry for imposing on you again.

06:13.530 --> 06:15.180
Did you bring my pay?

06:15.180 --> 06:17.390
Yes. It's right here.

06:18.310 --> 06:23.540
Hm... Since you paid, you may impose on me.

06:24.390 --> 06:26.180
And what about my tip?

06:27.710 --> 06:30.020
The latest cake from Meifudo.

06:30.020 --> 06:31.160
Will this suffice?

06:31.450 --> 06:33.660
Oh, that place, huh?

06:33.660 --> 06:36.890
<i>One offering of luxury pastries per job.</i>

06:36.890 --> 06:40.080
<i>That's the tip required to get 
Otoi-san to work for us.</i>

06:40.550 --> 06:43.160
<i>When I tried negotiating payment with her...</i>

06:43.160 --> 06:44.090
Payment?

06:45.110 --> 06:48.250
I do this for fun. I don't accept payment.

06:48.250 --> 06:52.650
<i>In other words, she doesn't consider this work, 
so there's no responsibility involved...</i>

06:52.650 --> 06:55.450
I'm not feeling it today. Pass.

06:55.450 --> 07:00.170
<i>...so things like that have happened before. 
But we have a schedule to keep, so...</i>

07:00.170 --> 07:03.370
What if I bring you luxury 
pastries for each job?

07:03.370 --> 07:04.330
Hmm...

07:05.620 --> 07:08.560
<i>That's the contract I managed to seal with her,</i>

07:08.560 --> 07:11.110
<i>but she can be fickle.</i>

07:11.390 --> 07:15.620
<i>There have been times when she refused 
because she didn't like the pastries I brought.</i>

07:15.620 --> 07:18.300
Okay, this looks tasty.

07:18.300 --> 07:20.300
I'll work for you today.

07:21.950 --> 07:24.460
Senpai, I'll head into the booth.

07:24.460 --> 07:26.270
Could I get the script?

07:26.270 --> 07:27.340
Oh, sure.

07:29.770 --> 07:33.010
You always push things 
to the extreme, don't you, Aki?

07:33.010 --> 07:34.050
What do you mean?

07:34.050 --> 07:38.830
Most people would give the actor 
their script days in advance.

07:38.830 --> 07:43.810
If you told a real voice actor to just 
jump in with no rehearsal, they'd kill you.

07:44.160 --> 07:45.860
Yeah, but as you know,

07:45.860 --> 07:49.030
her home environment made her 
the freak of nature she is.

07:49.370 --> 07:52.640
Oh, right, because her mom hates showbiz.

07:52.640 --> 07:53.520
Right.

07:53.520 --> 07:55.850
So... five minutes, was it?

07:55.850 --> 08:00.700
Yes. She only needs to read a script 
for five minutes to act it out flawlessly.

08:01.160 --> 08:04.750
Growing up in misfortune 
fosters brilliance, huh?

08:05.190 --> 08:07.170
I guess it does happen.

08:07.170 --> 08:10.410
<i>She's recording voices 
for five characters today,</i>

08:10.410 --> 08:13.010
<i>including some very unique 
male and female voices.</i>

08:13.010 --> 08:14.430
<i>But I'm not worried.</i>

08:14.870 --> 08:17.000
<i>I know Iroha can make it look effortless.</i>

08:14.870 --> 08:17.000
Time to get started.

08:17.000 --> 08:18.810
Kohinata, you ready?

08:18.810 --> 08:21.080
Yes, anytime!

08:21.080 --> 08:24.900
I'll do my best to put on some 
good acting for you, Senpai!

08:24.900 --> 08:28.940
The first one we're recording is a burly 
delinquent guy who does whatever he wants.

08:29.310 --> 08:30.560
<i>Okay, go.</i>

08:33.650 --> 08:38.990
From here on in, you're settin' 
foot on <i>my</i> turf! Hyah-ha!

08:39.740 --> 08:42.210
When they say "eager for battle," 
"ruler of the nine hells,"

08:42.210 --> 08:44.330
"I alone am supreme 
throughout Heaven and Earth,"

08:44.330 --> 08:47.120
and "got the looks and the brains to match,"

08:47.120 --> 08:48.210
they're talkin' about me!

08:48.210 --> 08:49.280
Wha...

08:49.710 --> 08:52.140
Whoever wants to die first, come at me!

08:52.140 --> 08:55.010
My chainsaw's so excited, it's breathin' fire!

08:57.830 --> 09:00.850
Hey, Kohinata. Can I ask you something?

09:01.100 --> 09:02.810
Sure! What is it?

09:03.180 --> 09:06.990
Why does this delinquent sound 
like a prim and proper young lady?

09:07.830 --> 09:11.610
Is something wrong? Is that not how it should be?

09:11.970 --> 09:13.100
Hm...

09:13.660 --> 09:15.700
Let's try another character.

09:15.970 --> 09:17.280
<i>Sure thing!</i>

09:17.280 --> 09:20.360
I'll always be watching you, Onii-chan.

09:20.360 --> 09:22.930
I've made up my mind 
to never leave your side.

09:22.930 --> 09:23.660
<i>Next character.</i>

09:24.190 --> 09:28.100
It's not good to think of 
everything negatively.

09:28.100 --> 09:28.670
<i>Next.</i>

09:28.670 --> 09:31.630
I can't back down now!

09:37.210 --> 09:39.090
What the hell? Is she playing with us?

09:42.100 --> 09:45.100
<b>MY FRIEND'S LITTLE SISTER HAS IT IN FOR ME!</b>

09:50.770 --> 09:54.940
I'm sorry! I know her acting skills 
are better than this!

09:54.940 --> 09:58.490
I know that. Man, what a drag.

09:59.560 --> 10:03.480
<i>Hey, Kohinata. Are you happy 
with your acting right now?</i>

10:03.480 --> 10:06.480
Of course! I know it'll get the okay!

10:06.480 --> 10:08.210
After all, it's 100% tailored

10:08.210 --> 10:10.000
<i>to my producer's tastes!</i>

10:10.920 --> 10:13.130
Okay, Iroha, stop screwing around!

10:14.140 --> 10:16.300
<i>You know you can't do that, Iroha!</i>

10:16.300 --> 10:19.290
<i>Sure, I might've made you 
feel bad on a personal level,</i>

10:19.290 --> 10:22.260
<i>and I know that's my fault. 
I can't even make excuses.</i>

10:22.260 --> 10:27.310
<i>But you can't belittle the path 
you've chosen to take in life!</i>

10:27.770 --> 10:30.270
Iroha, you—

10:32.200 --> 10:33.270
Hold up.

10:41.750 --> 10:45.850
<i>Okay, that's it. We're done. 
Studio's closed for the day.</i>

10:45.850 --> 10:48.210
<i>We'll try this again after 
we've all cooled down.</i>

10:48.690 --> 10:49.680
Okay.

10:57.750 --> 10:59.470
What a pain.

10:59.470 --> 11:02.170
Otoi-san, thank you for doing this.

11:02.170 --> 11:03.640
And I'm sorry.

11:04.120 --> 11:08.890
If you hadn't given me this, I might've 
said something I couldn't take back.

11:09.570 --> 11:12.030
So, what happened?

11:12.030 --> 11:15.740
I gave you an indirect kiss, 
so you can tell me, right?

11:19.890 --> 11:21.700
I see.

11:22.220 --> 11:25.080
Good for you, you normie.

11:25.080 --> 11:29.710
If I were a normie, I probably would've 
handled all this in a smarter way.

11:29.710 --> 11:32.000
This is a lot of firsts for me.

11:32.000 --> 11:34.510
Frankly, I'm just being 
toyed with from all sides.

11:35.890 --> 11:39.440
That's funny. You're the one 
being toyed with now.

11:39.440 --> 11:41.260
Miracles do happen.

11:41.260 --> 11:43.390
Are you in any position to say that?

11:44.100 --> 11:45.950
I'm exactly in the position to say it.

11:45.950 --> 11:48.640
I've always thought of toying 
with people as my specialty.

11:49.020 --> 11:54.320
I don't know much about love, though, and 
I don't know what Kohinata's really thinking.

11:54.320 --> 11:56.110
The one thing I will say is...

11:56.110 --> 12:00.620
If you crush Kohinata's talent, 
I'll make you regret it.

12:02.030 --> 12:05.970
I love music, and I love working with sound.

12:05.970 --> 12:10.000
I like to think I have pretty keen ears,

12:10.000 --> 12:13.150
but I don't have what it takes to be an artist.

12:13.150 --> 12:15.950
I'm not showy enough, 
and I don't have the natural talent.

12:16.370 --> 12:18.670
I know that <i>because</i> I have such keen ears.

12:20.200 --> 12:24.190
That's why I made up my mind 
to stay in a supporting role.

12:24.190 --> 12:26.260
I want to lend my skills 
to help a true prodigy

12:26.260 --> 12:29.050
grow from one-in-a-thousand 
to one-in-a-million.

12:29.710 --> 12:32.930
And that prodigy is Kohinata.

12:33.390 --> 12:36.050
Her acting is just... I don't know.

12:36.050 --> 12:38.480
It's like she's channeling 
the character's spirit.

12:38.480 --> 12:39.400
Yeah.

12:39.790 --> 12:45.670
You know, I'm willing to devote 
the rest of my time in high school to her.

12:46.360 --> 12:50.640
I wouldn't let her use this fancy studio 
for a few sweets otherwise.

12:47.660 --> 12:52.410
<i>Otoi-san and I are just pitiful believers 
charmed by Iroha's talent.</i>

12:52.870 --> 12:53.750
Which is why...

12:54.260 --> 12:58.210
if you destroy Kohinata's talent 
with some stupid teenage drama,

12:58.790 --> 13:00.710
I'll make you regret it for life.

13:03.240 --> 13:05.870
That Mashiro girl must be pretty cute.

13:06.600 --> 13:07.970
I don't know...

13:07.970 --> 13:10.960
Oh, come on. It's obvious she is.

13:10.960 --> 13:13.950
You've never shown any
 outward interest in girls,

13:13.950 --> 13:16.560
and you've agonized over her 
rather than rejecting her outright.

13:16.560 --> 13:18.890
That's 100% proof that she's cute.

13:18.890 --> 13:20.740
Were you even listening?

13:20.740 --> 13:23.170
I made a deal with 
President Tsukinomori!

13:23.170 --> 13:26.990
But you can't prove that that's not just 
an excuse you're giving yourself, can you?

13:27.250 --> 13:28.870
Well, I...

13:31.220 --> 13:33.370
You're too tense.

13:33.680 --> 13:34.410
C'mere.

13:39.460 --> 13:40.490
Whoa, wait—

13:41.100 --> 13:43.970
Adolescence is pointless. You don't need it.

13:43.970 --> 13:46.260
You don't understand romantic feelings, either.

13:46.790 --> 13:48.560
I'm the same way.

13:49.730 --> 13:53.980
But listen close. 
Can you hear my heart beating?

13:55.140 --> 13:57.080
It's going really fast now, huh?

13:58.620 --> 14:04.990
Even a girl with values like mine can't 
remain unaffected in a situation like this.

14:05.690 --> 14:09.660
I know I'm not the type to really 
show it on my face, though.

14:11.530 --> 14:13.390
You're the same way, aren't you?

14:13.390 --> 14:14.330
Am I?

14:14.330 --> 14:15.890
You don't want anything pointless.

14:15.890 --> 14:19.420
You might think that, 
but when you actually experience it,

14:19.420 --> 14:21.400
your body reacts on its own.

14:22.030 --> 14:26.050
Humans are animals too, you know. It happens.

14:26.050 --> 14:29.960
You're saying that's just how much 
Mashiro's confession affected me?

14:29.960 --> 14:32.300
Both me and Iroha?

14:33.230 --> 14:35.250
<i>She might be right.</i>

14:35.250 --> 14:39.380
<i>I didn't take the most efficient route. 
I didn't even try to.</i>

14:39.380 --> 14:42.730
<i>I tried to strike a balance that would 
hurt everyone as little as possible</i>

14:42.730 --> 14:46.520
<i>as a way of taking control 
so that things would end</i>

14:46.520 --> 14:48.700
<i>in the outcome that suited me best.</i>

14:49.150 --> 14:50.950
Thanks, Otoi-san.

14:51.210 --> 14:53.450
You helped me remember my roots.

14:54.210 --> 14:58.120
I like that look in your eyes. 
I bet you could talk to her now.

14:58.540 --> 15:00.330
Yeah, I think I can.

15:01.320 --> 15:03.460
About today, um...

15:03.460 --> 15:05.020
I'm sorry.

15:05.020 --> 15:06.670
Eh, don't worry about it.

15:07.820 --> 15:11.050
But I'll be expecting my 
payment next time, too.

15:11.050 --> 15:13.800
You don't miss a beat, do you?

15:16.770 --> 15:19.770
<b>I CAN'T WAIT FOR THE DAY I CAN REVEAL IT!</b>

15:16.770 --> 15:19.770
<b>\h
LET'S GET DINNER TOGETHER TONIGHT. 
I'LL SEND YOU THE TIME AND PLACE LATER. 
I'LL GIVE YOU MY ANSWER
TO YOUR CONFESSION THEN.</b>

15:28.450 --> 15:30.380
D-Don't laugh!

15:30.380 --> 15:33.660
Sorry. You just look so nervous, 
it's kinda funny.

15:33.960 --> 15:37.910
Shut up! It's your fault for getting 
reservations at a place like this!

15:38.180 --> 15:40.750
Are you sure we should be eating 
at a place this expensive?

15:40.750 --> 15:43.970
I could get my dad to cover it for us.

15:43.970 --> 15:49.170
What kind of scumbag would I be if 
I asked my date's dad to pay for our dinner?

15:49.190 --> 15:53.510
You just don't know 
how to handle girls, do you?

15:54.310 --> 15:56.220
You don't have to worry about the money.

15:56.220 --> 15:57.730
The business will cover it.

15:57.730 --> 15:58.560
It will?

15:58.560 --> 16:01.880
05th Floor Alliance has made 
pretty decent money, you know.

16:01.880 --> 16:03.940
I wouldn't waste it on myself,

16:03.940 --> 16:06.520
but if it's for the team, 
I'll spend as much as it takes.

16:06.520 --> 16:11.410
But I'm, um... not helping you 
make your game.

16:11.410 --> 16:12.530
Am I?

16:12.820 --> 16:17.950
Yeah. But while I can't say why, 
this dinner isn't unrelated to our business.

16:17.950 --> 16:19.140
Um...

16:19.140 --> 16:21.370
Don't worry about the details.

16:21.890 --> 16:23.870
Let's just enjoy our meal.

16:23.870 --> 16:25.520
O-Okay.

16:25.520 --> 16:28.920
Is this wine? Um, I can't...

16:28.920 --> 16:32.610
It's the restaurant's recommendation: 
non-alcoholic wine.

16:32.610 --> 16:35.790
Also known as... grape juice.

16:37.410 --> 16:38.510
Cheers.

16:38.510 --> 16:40.060
Ch-Cheers.

16:42.690 --> 16:43.480
It's good.

16:43.480 --> 16:44.750
Right?

16:44.750 --> 16:46.150
This restaurant...

16:47.030 --> 16:48.810
attracts a lot of couples.

16:48.810 --> 16:51.190
Well, yeah, it's that kind of place.

16:51.480 --> 16:53.320
Do you dislike this type of restaurant?

16:53.320 --> 16:54.200
No!

16:54.500 --> 16:57.060
I can look at the couples and 
not feel overcome with hatred.

16:57.060 --> 16:58.480
This is a first!

16:58.480 --> 17:00.790
Just how much do you hate couples?

17:00.790 --> 17:05.130
Well, they just act so happy. 
It's like they're showing off.

17:05.130 --> 17:10.110
Like they're making fun of me, saying, 
"You're all alone, huh? Poor thing."

17:10.110 --> 17:13.170
Well, I do get where 
you're coming from, I guess.

17:13.170 --> 17:15.260
But it's not like that, is it?

17:15.680 --> 17:20.680
Those happy-looking couples 
weren't laughing at me.

17:21.100 --> 17:25.190
In fact, they weren't thinking 
about anyone else at all.

17:25.520 --> 17:29.710
I never understood that 
until I fell in love myself.

17:38.190 --> 17:39.160
It's beautiful.

17:39.160 --> 17:39.900
Yeah.

17:40.490 --> 17:42.020
I'm glad I came.

17:42.020 --> 17:46.410
You were so reluctant at first, 
I thought maybe you were afraid of heights.

17:46.410 --> 17:48.000
I'm not. It's just...

18:03.770 --> 18:04.930
Hey, Mashiro...

18:07.430 --> 18:08.350
Yeah?

18:08.350 --> 18:11.890
Let me give you my answer to your confession. 
That's the point of this date.

18:11.890 --> 18:14.110
It's okay. I don't need an answer.

18:14.670 --> 18:16.350
No, let me say it!

18:16.350 --> 18:19.980
I faced my own feelings in earnest 
after hearing how you felt.

18:19.980 --> 18:22.780
If I don't get to respond to you, 
I'll regret it forever!

18:23.460 --> 18:26.450
I thought you'd say that. 
You're always so pushy.

18:26.450 --> 18:27.540
But that's not right.

18:27.880 --> 18:28.940
It's not?

18:30.520 --> 18:34.670
You're about to reject me, aren't you?

18:36.090 --> 18:38.050
What made you think that?

18:38.050 --> 18:39.340
I can tell.

18:39.340 --> 18:44.570
You wanted to give me this 
beautiful memory and end it with that.

18:44.570 --> 18:47.140
From the moment you sent me that message,

18:47.140 --> 18:49.570
I knew you were going to turn me down.

18:49.570 --> 18:51.710
Because you're so kind.

18:51.710 --> 18:52.920
You're wrong!

18:53.370 --> 18:56.340
It's because if I make you feel bad and
 break the fake-girlfriend contract,

18:56.340 --> 18:59.060
I'll lose my connection 
to President Tsukinomori!

18:59.550 --> 19:04.500
I opted for the solution that would 
be best for 05th Floor Alliance.

19:05.070 --> 19:07.480
All to suit myself. That's not kindness.

19:09.800 --> 19:14.520
Aki, you have no idea how much I love you.

19:14.520 --> 19:17.460
That's why you think 
you can fool me so easily.

19:18.170 --> 19:19.760
But I won't be fooled.

19:19.760 --> 19:22.610
You're doing this for me because you're kind.

19:22.610 --> 19:26.970
No matter how much you deny it, 
the truth inside me won't change.

19:26.970 --> 19:28.240
Mashiro...

19:28.240 --> 19:30.720
It's obvious when I really think about it.

19:30.720 --> 19:34.280
I mean, Iroha-chan is so cute, 
but she's not your girlfriend.

19:34.280 --> 19:37.400
If a girl like her is that close to you 
and you haven't fallen for her,

19:37.820 --> 19:41.990
it's not like you'd even waver when 
I re-entered your life after so long.

19:42.410 --> 19:46.100
I knew I was just getting 
carried away on my own.

19:46.100 --> 19:48.810
05th Floor Alliance comes first for you.

19:48.810 --> 19:51.870
You have no interest 
in a relationship with me at all.

19:51.870 --> 19:54.640
But still, I wanted to move forward.

19:54.640 --> 19:56.630
I wanted you to know how I felt.

19:56.970 --> 19:58.900
That's why I told you.

19:58.900 --> 20:01.330
I've been running away for so long.

20:01.330 --> 20:04.010
I thought I might be able to change myself.

20:04.930 --> 20:07.310
I wanted to take just one more step.

20:07.560 --> 20:08.470
So...

20:09.190 --> 20:11.310
I'm content with this for now.

20:11.310 --> 20:12.980
I made a move, and that's a win.

20:14.540 --> 20:17.780
All I want to hear is an "okay."

20:17.780 --> 20:21.140
So I don't need an answer from you right now.

20:21.140 --> 20:23.910
I don't know how many 
months or years it'll take,

20:25.170 --> 20:29.410
but I <i>will</i> make you love me one day.

20:33.250 --> 20:37.210
There's no guarantee 
that I'll grow to love you.

20:37.730 --> 20:40.420
It'd be more efficient to forget me 
and move on to someone else.

20:40.850 --> 20:43.940
Are you stupid? Some min-maxer you are.

20:43.940 --> 20:44.410
Huh?

20:44.410 --> 20:46.400
Take the shortest route to your goal.

20:46.400 --> 20:48.290
That's what a min-maxer does, right?

20:48.290 --> 20:50.850
My goal isn't to get a boyfriend.

20:51.180 --> 20:53.290
It's to make <i>you</i> my boyfriend.

20:53.290 --> 20:56.520
In terms of efficiency, 
giving up is out of the question.

20:56.890 --> 20:59.370
I have my hands full 
with 05th Floor Alliance.

20:59.370 --> 21:01.950
I don't know when things 
will calm down for us.

21:02.460 --> 21:04.400
It'll probably be after we graduate.

21:04.820 --> 21:07.370
By that time, you won't still be around me—

21:07.370 --> 21:08.100
I will.

21:08.620 --> 21:11.790
For as long as you stay 
with 05th Floor Alliance,

21:11.790 --> 21:14.180
I'll be near you, without a doubt.

21:14.630 --> 21:20.010
So I'll get to stay by your side 
until everything is resolved.

21:21.180 --> 21:23.070
I'll head home.

21:23.070 --> 21:25.160
I must be making you feel awkward.

21:25.160 --> 21:28.510
But starting tomorrow, I'll be coming on 
to you so hard, it'll drive you nuts.

21:30.360 --> 21:32.520
You'd better be ready, Aki.

21:45.070 --> 21:46.320
<b>IROHA</b>

21:47.450 --> 21:49.310
<i>Sorry I made you wait, Iroha.</i>

21:49.310 --> 21:50.840
<i>You're next.</i>

21:51.740 --> 21:55.620
